  "caption_groups": [
    {
      "start": 0.852083,
      "end": 2.688041,
      "text": "In Europe, beavers were reduced to"
    },
    {
      "start": 2.714083,
      "end": 5.005749,
      "text": "fragmented populations, with combined"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.01875,
      "end": 7.323458,
      "text": "population numbers being estimated across"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.336458,
      "end": 8.781790999999998,
      "text": "multiple river basins."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.504083,
      "end": 12.782748999999999,
      "text": "Beavers live in freshwater ecosystems such"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.795749999999998,
      "end": 15.360873999999999,
      "text": "as rivers, streams, lakes and ponds across"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.386916,
      "end": 17.756707,
      "text": "their native geographic distribution ranges."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.084083,
      "end": 21.505958,
      "text": "The concept became popular in conservation,"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.792416,
      "end": 23.133582,
      "text": "and was deployed in a range of"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.159625,
      "end": 25.503375,
      "text": "contexts to engender support for protecting"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.529415999999998,
      "end": 26.245582,
      "text": "habitats."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.568082999999998,
      "end": 29.950916,
      "text": "Human activities had damaged ecosystems,"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.133207999999996,
      "end": 32.34675,
      "text": "such as by removing keystone predators that"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.372791,
      "end": 34.299875,
      "text": "previously maintained balance in those"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.325916,
      "end": 35.536875,
      "text": "natural environments."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.86808299999999,
      "end": 39.276956999999996,
      "text": "In addition, wolves often kept animals from"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.30299999999999,
      "end": 40.839456999999996,
      "text": "grazing in riparian areas,"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.12591599999999,
      "end": 42.94883299999999,
      "text": "which protected beavers from having their"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.96183299999999,
      "end": 44.60245799999999,
      "text": "food sources encroached upon."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.92808299999999,
      "end": 47.64683199999998,
      "text": "The connectivity of streams to their"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.67287499999998,
      "end": 49.717165999999985,
      "text": "adjacent floodplain along their entire"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.74320799999999,
      "end": 51.448956999999986,
      "text": "length plays an important role in the"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.47495799999999,
      "end": 53.310915999999985,
      "text": "equilibrium of the river system."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.65208299999998,
      "end": 56.94379099999998,
      "text": "Stream restoration or river restoration,"
    },
    {
      "start": 57.139082999999985,
      "end": 59.027124999999984,
      "text": "sometimes called river reclamation in the"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.04012499999998,
      "end": 61.24066599999998,
      "text": "United Kingdom, is a set of activities"
    },
    {
      "start": 61.26666599999999,
      "end": 63.37604099999998,
      "text": "that aim to improve environmental health."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.72008299999997,
      "end": 66.63416599999998,
      "text": "However, it is important to note that"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.66020799999998,
      "end": 68.47012499999998,
      "text": "these groups do not cover the entire"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.49612499999998,
      "end": 70.149791,
      "text": "range known to be occupied by the"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.17583299999998,
      "end": 71.25654099999998,
      "text": "subspecies today."
    }
  ],
